From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: fast translate, cheaper shader translation with the same SPIR-V (EDEN_UP_FAST_TRANSLATE)

DRAFT, not built. Port of Djihads80's work (Djihads80/Eglantine PR #825: e4197fb88 SSA definitions
in blocks, 398dfbc1d scalar constant ids remembered, 87b0f018a failed storage-buffer searches
pruned), read from zortos293/Lichii PR #1320 by StiensWout. Gated by EDEN_UP_FAST_TRANSLATE=1
(boot, not a live switch); off by default. EDEN_UP_FAST_TRANSLATE_VERIFY=1 (boot) runs the old and
the new way side by side and counts differences (ssa, storage buffers, constants). Both names are
in vk_pipeline_prep's TranslationSwitches (the shader-store stamp): a run with either picks its own
prepared-shader store. Not gated: 192 bytes per IR::Block. New file shader_recompiler/fast_translate.h.

Reviewed draft (ports review, verdict "ready with corrections"): shader-translate-speed.v2.patch;
all +/- lines byte-identical, context unchanged.
